{
  "__inputs": [
    {
      "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
      "label": "Prometheus",
      "description": "",
      "type": "datasource",
      "pluginId": "prometheus",
      "pluginName": "Prometheus"
    }
  ],
  "__requires": [
    {
      "type": "grafana",
      "id": "grafana",
      "name": "Grafana",
      "version": "10.0.0"
    },
    {
      "type": "datasource",
      "id": "prometheus",
      "name": "Prometheus",
      "version": "1.0.0"
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "stat",
      "name": "Stat",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "timeseries",
      "name": "Time series",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "text",
      "name": "Text",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "panel",
      "id": "row",
      "name": "Row",
      "version": ""
    }
  ],
  "id": null,
  "uid": "turnstile-fairness",
  "title": "Turnstile: fairness & scheduler health",
  "description": "Who is waiting, how long, why, and whether the fairness policy is actually doing its job. Fed by METRICS_ADDR=:PORT go test -bench Scheduler (see scheduler_test.go).",
  "tags": [
    "turnstile",
    "llm",
    "fairness",
    "scheduler"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "5s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {},
        "hide": 0,
        "label": "Prometheus"
      },
      {
        "name": "run",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(turnstile_requests_total, run)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "label": "run"
      },
      {
        "name": "policy",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(turnstile_requests_total, policy)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "label": "policy"
      },
      {
        "name": "model",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(turnstile_requests_total, model)",
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "label": "model"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this in 10 seconds",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Top row = the only thing you need to glance at.** Everything red means something is actually broken; everything green/grey means turnstile is doing its job.\n\n- **Stuck tenants** > 0 -> the ring-buffer/map bug class: jobs are queued for a tenant that dropped out of the rotation. They will never be served. This should never be non-zero.\n- **Oldest queued job** rising -> starvation: someone has been waiting too long. Compressed benchmark runs: anything over ~1s is suspicious; real traffic: the plan's own alert fires at 20s.\n- **Worst fairness index** near 0 -> one tenant is taking an unfair share of a model (0=totally unfair, 1=perfectly fair). Near 1 is the whole point of this project. Caveat: a clean green **1.00** can also mean *no data* (no tenant has used that model recently) rather than 'perfectly fair' - check the fairness-per-model panel below if the tile looks suspiciously perfect.\n- **Rejected (buffer full)** > 0 -> the model's tenant slots are exhausted; new tenants for that model are being turned away.\n- **Models gate-closed** -> how many models are currently throttled by their own provider TPM limit. Not a bug by itself, just means those models are maxed out.\n- **Served %** -> share of all requests that got a real answer instead of a timeout, rejection or error. Under the benchmark's `noisy=true` scenario this settles around 64-65% **by design** - the flood tenant is meant to get throttled once its model's gate closes, so red here during a noisy run isn't a regression."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Stuck Tenants (ring buffer bug)",
      "description": "Counts models where jobs are queued in the tenant map but the tenant has no slot in the ring buffer: those jobs will never be dispatched. This is the exact bug class fixed in d8e9b46. Should always read 0; any non-zero value is a live instance of that bug.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "count(turnstile_queue_jobs{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"} > 0 unless turnstile_queue_tenants{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"} > 0) OR vector(0)",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Oldest Queued Job",
      "description": "Age of the single longest-waiting job across all models right now. Rises before timeouts start, so it's the earliest starvation warning. 20s is the production alert threshold from the telemetry plan; in a 500x-compressed benchmark run, anything sustained above ~1s is already worth a look.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "max(turnstile_queue_oldest_job_age_seconds{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}) OR vector(0)",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 20
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Worst Fairness Index",
      "description": "Lowest Jain's fairness index across all selected models (1.0 = every tenant's token share is equal, toward 1/n = one tenant is taking almost everything). Caution: 1.00 can also mean 'no data' - either no tenant has used that model in the last 60s, or nothing currently matches $model/$policy/$run - not necessarily 'perfectly fair'. Cross-check against the Fairness index per model panel below before trusting a green 1.00.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "min(turnstile_fairness_index{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}) OR vector(1)",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.3
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.7
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Rejected (buffer full) /s",
      "description": "Requests per second turned away with 'ring buffer full capacity' - a model's fixed number of tenant slots are all taken by other tenants. Any sustained non-zero value means that model needs more ring buffer capacity (bufSize) or is seeing more distinct tenants than it was sized for.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(turnstile_requests_total{outcome=\"rejected_queue_full\", model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval])) OR vector(0)",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.001
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Models Gate-Closed",
      "description": "How many of the selected models currently have their soft TPM gate closed (95% of the provider's tokens-per-minute limit used up in the last 60s). Not a bug by itself - it just means those models are maxed out and dispatch is paused for everyone until usage ages out of the window.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "count(turnstile_model_gate_open{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"} == 0) OR vector(0)",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Served %",
      "description": "Share of all requests that got outcome=served instead of a timeout, rejection or LLM error. Heads up: under the benchmark's noisy=true scenario this settles around 64-65% BY DESIGN - the flood tenant's excess requests are meant to time out once its model's TPM gate closes, so red here during noisy=true is expected, not a regression. The thresholds assume a noisy=false / production baseline; lower them if you're watching a noisy=true run specifically.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 20,
        "y": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "100 * sum(rate(turnstile_requests_total{outcome=\"served\", model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum(rate(turnstile_requests_total{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 90
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 98
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Fairness \u2014 is every tenant getting a fair share?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Fairness index per model (1.0 = perfectly fair)",
      "description": "Jain's fairness index over each tenant's tokens in the last 60s. Drops toward 1/n when one tenant dominates a model.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "turnstile_fairness_index{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{model}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Top 5 tenants by token rate (busiest model)",
      "description": "The noisy-neighbour check: one line far above the rest means one tenant is hogging a model's tokens.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "topk(5, sum by (tenant) (rate(turnstile_tokens_total{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{tenant}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Requests served per tenant per minute",
      "description": "If fairness works, lines for tenants on the same tier should sit close together even while one tenant floods the model.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "60 * sum by (tenant) (rate(turnstile_requests_total{outcome=\"served\", model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{tenant}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Queue & latency",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue wait, p50/p95/p99 (dispatched jobs only)",
      "description": "How long a dispatched job sat in the ring buffer before its turn, at three percentiles. A rising p99 with a flat p50 means a tail of tenants is waiting much longer than the typical request - worth cross-checking against Oldest Queued Job and the fairness index for the same model.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le, model) (rate(turnstile_queue_wait_seconds_bucket{dispatched=\"true\", model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{model}} p50"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, model) (rate(turnstile_queue_wait_seconds_bucket{dispatched=\"true\", model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "refId": "B",
          "legendFormat": "{{model}} p95"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, model) (rate(turnstile_queue_wait_seconds_bucket{dispatched=\"true\", model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "refId": "C",
          "legendFormat": "{{model}} p99"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "End-to-end request duration, p99 by outcome",
      "description": "p99 latency as the caller sees it: queue wait + worker wait + the LLM call itself, split by how the request ended. This is what the benchmark's own p99-ms metric approximates for outcome=served.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 27
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le, outcome) (rate(turnstile_request_duration_seconds_bucket{model=~\"$model\", policy=~\"$policy\", run=~\"$run\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}} p99"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "pointSize": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
